  "bug_report_content": "Title: Comparing with NaN is incorrect\nType: Bug | Priority: Major | Status: Resolved | Resolution: Fixed\n\nDescription:\n'NaN' > 'NaN' is true, but should be FALSE\n\nComments:\n\n[Matthew Jason Benson]: Whoops!  Never screwed around with NaN before, apparently... Thanks for the catch, fixed in trunk.  :)\n\n[Sergey Vladimirov]: assertXPathValue(context, \"$nan = 1\", Boolean.FALSE, Boolean.class);\n+        assertXPathValue(context, \"$nan != 1\", Boolean.TRUE, Boolean.class);\n\nNaN  != 1 => FALSE\n\n[Matthew Jason Benson]: Whew!  You are keeping me on my toes, certainly!  Fixed part 2 in trunk.",
  "fix_diff": "--- org.apache.commons.jxpath.ri.compiler.CoreOperationRelationalExpression (buggy)\n+++ org.apache.commons.jxpath.ri.compiler.CoreOperationRelationalExpression (fixed)\n@@ -73,7 +73,13 @@\n             return containsMatch((Iterator) right, left);\n         }\n         double ld = InfoSetUtil.doubleValue(left);\n+        if (Double.isNaN(ld)) {\n+            return false;\n+        }\n         double rd = InfoSetUtil.doubleValue(right);\n+        if (Double.isNaN(rd)) {\n+            return false;\n+        }\n         return evaluateCompare(ld == rd ? 0 : ld < rd ? -1 : 1);\n     }"
}